1. Claim 15 (Currently amended): A method for selecting an edge server computer from a plurality of server computers for sending data to a client computer, the method comprising the steps of:
accessing a server computer through a path in a computer network, the path including one or more server computers;
adding information indicative of at least one server computer of the first set of one or more server computers to a locator of a resource on a second server computer, the resource having a unique signature as part of its identifier, wherein the information is added by a media request broker that analyzes server load and availability metrics;
selecting the first server computer based on the information added to the locator, wherein the selection is performed by the media request broker in response to a media request containing the unique signature.

2. Claim 16 (Currently amended): The method of claim 15, the second server computer being a Web application server comprising a Web page with a hyperlink referencing the data to be sent to the client computer, the hyperlink including a unique signature, the method further comprising the steps of selecting the hyperlink by the client computer, subsequently generating an http request out of this hyperlink by a web browser, this http request containing the unique signature identifying a media request, and __providing the unique signature and associated server load information to the media request broker, wherein the media request broker uses the unique signature to identify and select the first server computer based on real-time server performance metrics__.

3. Claim 17 (Original): (Previously presented)

4. Claim 18 (Currently amended): The method of claim 17, the media request broker selecting the first server computer based on the information __by comparing server load metrics and availability data associated with each server computer in the plurality of server computers and selecting the server computer with the lowest load or highest availability__.

5. Claim 24 (Currently amended): A system for selecting an edge server computer from a plurality of server computers for sending data to a client computer, the system comprising:
a client computer;
a plurality of server computers accessible through a path in a computer network;
a media request broker configured to add information indicative of at least one server computer of the first set of one or more server computers to a locator of a resource on a second server computer, the resource having a unique signature as part of its identifier, wherein the information comprises server load and availability metrics;
circuitry for selecting the first server computer based on the information added to the locator, wherein the selection is performed by the media request broker in response to a media request containing the unique signature.

6. Claim 25 (Currently amended): The system of claim 24, the second server computer being a Web application server comprising a Web page with a hyperlink referencing the data to be sent to the client computer, the hyperlink including a unique signature, the system further comprising circuitry for selecting the hyperlink by the client computer, and subsequently generating an http request out of this hyperlink by a web browser, this http request containing the unique signature identifying a media request, and __circuitry for providing the unique signature and associated server load information to the media request broker, wherein the media request broker uses the unique signature to identify and select the first server computer based on real-time server performance metrics__.

7. Claim 27 (Currently amended): A computer program product for selecting an edge server computer from a plurality of server computers for sending data to a client computer, the computer program product comprising:
a computer-readable medium;
program code on the computer-readable medium for accessing a server computer through a path in a computer network, the path including one or more server computers;
program code for adding information indicative of at least one server computer of the first set of one or more server computers to a locator of a resource on a second server computer, the resource having a unique signature as part of its identifier, wherein the information is added by a media request broker that analyzes server load and availability metrics;
program code for selecting the first server computer based on the information added to the locator, wherein the selection is performed by the media request broker in response to a media request containing the unique signature.

8. Claim 28 (Currently amended): The computer program product of claim 27, the second server computer being a Web application server comprising a Web page with a hyperlink referencing the data to be sent to the client computer, the hyperlink including a unique signature, the computer program product further comprising the program step of selecting the hyperlink by the client computer, and subsequently generating an http request out of this hyperlink by a web browser, this http request containing the unique signature identifying a media request, and __providing the unique signature and associated server load information to the media request broker, wherein the media request broker uses the unique signature to identify and select the first server computer based on real-time server performance metrics__.
